    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Notes",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 32, "w": 24, "h": 4 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**p50/p95/p99** — These are percentiles of *mean execution time across distinct query shapes*, not per-invocation latency. A query that runs 10,000 times and averages 5ms counts as one data point at 5ms. For true per-invocation percentiles, wire up Prometheus + postgres_exporter (Phase 2).\n\n**Total time** — This shows where the database is spending the most cumulative wall-clock time. A fast query called 1M times can dominate here — that's where caching or batching pays off.\n\n**Reset stats** — `SELECT pg_stat_statements_reset();` clears all counters. Do this after a deploy or schema change to get a clean baseline."
      }
    }
  ],
